<title>USA: Newark air cargo rises 1.8 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Newark air cargo rises 1.8 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newark International Airport imported and exported 975,906 short tons of international and domestic air cargo in 1996, a 1.8 percent increase over the 958,419 short tons recorded in 1995, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said.</p>
<p>Mail at Newark during the same period fell 5.0 percent. It saw a 23.1 percent increase in international mail and an 8.9 percent in domestic traffic.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of air cargo and</p>
<p>mail at Newark in 1996 over 1995 with percentage changes:</p>
<p> Air Cargo	1996 short tons     1995	 Change</p>
<p> International	177,511	  179,767	-1.3</p>
<p> Domestic	     798,395	  778,652	 2.5</p>
<p> TOTAL		  975,906	  958,419	 1.8</p>
<p>Mail</p>
<p> International	 12,871	   10,452	23.1</p>
<p> Domestic		67,747	   74,366	-8.9</p>
<p> TOTAL		   80,618	   84,818	-5.0</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
